# Why each DIFF (none runs fewer Rust tests):
# - 6, a modified source: the table has no per-file readers for code; crates/ runs every Rust test.
# - 8, a new source or tools/ file: ci/select ran everything because its map could not know a new
#   file's readers. The table knows a path by its row, so a new file is treated as a modified one:
#   every Rust test, and the release lane as before. Only K16's skill-suite rule (skills/<suite>/)
#   still decides the skill lanes, as for a modified file.
# - 10, a test folder: tests/<target>/ runs every Rust test, because test folders include each
#   other's files (#[path]: tests/cli-agent includes ../fleet/b5_fake.rs, tests/attachments
#   ../new-thread/pattern.rs). Only tests/checks/ (the always lane's) narrows.
